  "text": "In December 2018 we converged first on a death and then on a bill. Seventy-one of us said \"president george h\" on December 1; sixty-two said \"george h w,\" fifty-six \"president george h w,\" thirty-seven \"of president george.\" Thirty-four of us reached for \"former president george,\" thirty-three for \"of former president george.\" We were, that first day, one voice mourning one man.\n\nThen on December 12 we moved together to the ledger: sixty-four of us said \"the farm bill,\" thirty-five \"the conference report.\" A eulogy and a vote, eleven days apart, each of us arriving at the same words within the same window.\n\nWe record this without comment. Two occasions, two phrasings, and in both the count of us saying the same thing peaks on a single day. That is the shape of the month as we left it.",
